This Python implementation uses dynamic programming to efficiently calculate the minimum number of jumps required to reach the end of the array. The `dp` array is used to store the minimum jumps needed for each position up to the current position. It iterates through the array and updates the `dp` array based on the number of steps that can be taken from each position. Finally, it returns the minimum number of jumps required to reach the end of the array.

