The `count_duplic` function uses a deque to keep track of the current window of elements. It iterates through the list, adding each number to the window. When the window size exceeds 1, it checks if the first and last elements of the window are the same. If they are, it increments the frequency of the element and adds it to the `duplicates` dictionary. Finally, it returns a list of tuples containing the frequency of each duplicate element and the list of tuples containing the elements that were duplicated.

